From 4cbdba0152c2975c3f44ad4233b7bb419cc3181f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allcodernet <67543055+allcodernet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:15:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/45] decide-score: full-path aggregation, temperature,
 variant averaging

score_field_full implements spec 4.1 from one node_logp row per trie
node (child log-probs aligned with the node's children, the END mass on
leaf rows, the MERGED mass per leaf child): log P(o) sums the child
log-probs along the option's path and ends with
log(p(t_k) * END(r_k) + MERGED(r_k-1)); the answer is P / sum P with
coverage = sum P, all in log space. A missing, duplicate or unaligned
row, a node out of range, NaN or +inf, a path that does not match the
trie nodes, or P = 0 for every option is a 500 engine error naming the
field.

rebuild_answer recomputes argmax (ties -> first) and expected from the
given probabilities and copies coverage, order_spread and given.
apply_temperature gives p_T proportional to exp(log p / T); T = 1
returns the input unchanged, T <= 0 or NaN is a 500 (0 is the options
struct's "not given"). average_variants takes the arithmetic mean of the
variants' probabilities and coverage, order_spread = max over options
of (max - min) over variants when there are 2 or more variants, and the
given of variant 0.

field_answer gains coverage and order_spread (NAN = not reported) and
given (null = not reported); answer_json adds them after the existing
keys only when set, so tree answers keep today's text (goldens checked
on the build before this change). score_field is unchanged.

test-decide-score: full-path P, P-hat and coverage to 1e-9 on hand-built
tries (a two-token and a one-token option with and without merged mass,
a branch below the root), the 500 cases, temperature at T = 1, 2, 0.5,
rebuild after T = 2 (score expected and confidence, bool p_true), debias
averaging and order_spread, answer_json goldens with and without the
new keys.
